IREE and StableHLO (OpenXLA backend, `xla-iree` feature only)
------------------------------------------------------------

No IREE or StableHLO source is vendored in this tree. The optional OpenXLA
backend emits StableHLO (https://github.com/openxla/stablehlo) graphs, and
under the off-by-default `xla-iree` cargo feature the C shim in
src/lib/mlxcel-xla/csrc/xla_iree.c is compiled against the IREE runtime
headers and linked against a prebuilt or source-built IREE runtime
(https://github.com/iree-org/iree), Copyright The IREE Authors, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions. `iree-compile`
from the same distribution lowers the emitted graphs ahead of time.

Release builds do not enable that feature, so shipped binaries contain no
IREE code. A locally built `xla-iree` binary statically links the IREE
runtime; the LLVM Exception to the Apache 2.0 License covers that Object
form embedding without the Section 4(a), 4(b), and 4(d) obligations, and
IREE ships a LICENSE with no NOTICE file, so nothing is carried forward
here. This section records the dependency.


